# Project Structure

Simplified medallion ETL + serving layout. See [domain-architecture.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/domain-architecture.mdc) for data flow and [tech-stack.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/tech-stack.mdc) for versions.

## Root Layout

```
binder_etl/
├── .cursor/rules/           # Architecture rules (SSOT for agents)
├── docker-compose.yaml      # MinIO + Postgres (Airflow meta) + Airflow
├── .env.example
├── requirements/
│   ├── spark.txt
│   └── airflow.txt
├── airbyte/
│   └── README.md            # abctl install + TikTok connection
├── dags/
│   └── tiktok/
│       └── tiktok_daily.py  # sync_raw → bronze → silver → gold → enrich
├── src/
│   ├── config/settings.py   # MinIO + BINDER_DATABASE_URL
│   ├── spark_session.py     # Spark + Delta + S3A
│   ├── io/
│   │   ├── reader.py        # Read Parquet/Delta from MinIO
│   │   ├── writer.py        # Write Delta to MinIO
│   │   └── postgres.py      # JDBC read Bridge + write serving
│   ├── pipelines/
│   │   └── run.py           # CLI: run {bronze|silver|gold|enrich} {platform}
│   └── transformers/
│       ├── base.py          # Thin shared base (one file)
│       └── tiktok/
│           ├── tables.py    # SSOT: streams, dedupe, join key contract
│           ├── bronze.py
│           ├── silver.py
│           ├── gold.py
│           └── enrich.py    # gold + Bridge → serving.metrics_daily
├── infra/
│   └── airflow/Dockerfile
└── tests/
    ├── test_spark_minio.py
    └── test_pipeline.py
```

**Deferred:** `src/api/` — serving tables satisfy dashboard reads for MVP.

**Backend follow-up:** `serving.metrics_daily` DDL in [binder_app_backend migrations](../binder_app_backend/src/system/database/migrations/); ETL owns enrich job only.

## Naming Conventions

| Item | Pattern | Example |
|------|---------|---------|
| Platform folder | lowercase slug | `tiktok`, `meta`, `google_ads` |
| Airflow DAG id | `{platform}_daily` | `tiktok_daily` |
| Airflow tasks | `{layer}_{platform}` | `bronze_tiktok`, `enrich_tiktok` |
| Raw path | `airbyte/{platform}/{stream}/` | `airbyte/tiktok/campaigns/` |
| Delta path | `{layer}/{platform}/{table}/` | `silver/tiktok/campaigns/` |
| Enrich module | `src/transformers/{platform}/enrich.py` | `tiktok/enrich.py` |
| Serving table | `serving.metrics_daily` | backend Postgres |
| Pipeline CLI | `run {layer} {platform}` | `run enrich tiktok` |
| Metadata SSOT | `src/transformers/{platform}/tables.py` | streams, dedupe, join keys |

## Entry Points

| File | Role |
|------|------|
| `src/pipelines/run.py` | CLI for bronze, silver, gold, enrich |
| `src/spark_session.py` | Spark session with Delta + MinIO S3A |
| `src/io/postgres.py` | JDBC helpers for Bridge read + serving write |
| `src/transformers/{platform}/tables.py` | Platform metadata single source of truth |
| `src/transformers/{platform}/enrich.py` | Gold + Bridge → serving cache |
| `dags/{platform}/{platform}_daily.py` | Airflow orchestration |

## Add a New Platform (Checklist)

1. Create `src/transformers/{platform}/tables.py` with streams, raw paths, dedupe keys, join key contract
2. Implement `bronze.py`, `silver.py`, `gold.py` extending shared `base.py`
3. Normalize silver to canonical columns: `ad_account_id`, `campaign_id`, `ad_group_id`, `ad_id` (all strings)
4. Implement `enrich.py` — join gold with Bridge, write `serving.metrics_daily`
5. Add platform to `PLATFORMS` list in pipeline runner
6. Create `dags/{platform}/{platform}_daily.py` with `enrich_{platform}` as final task
7. Document Airbyte connection in `airbyte/README.md`
8. Add smoke test under `tests/`

Copy the TikTok folder pattern — do not refactor shared code unless duplication exceeds ~30 lines.

## Simplification vs binder_data_hub

| Area | binder_data_hub | binder_etl |
|------|-----------------|------------|
| Base classes | `base_bronze.py`, `base_silver.py`, `base_gold.py` | Single `base.py` |
| Pipeline CLI | `run_layer` + legacy aliases | One `run.py` with enrich |
| Serving | Not implemented | `enrich.py` → backend Postgres |
| Query API | Full FastAPI catalog | Deferred (serving tables for MVP) |
| Docker | Multiple Dockerfiles | Shared image where possible |

`binder_data_hub` is inspiration only — do not copy its complexity.
